## Rework after the review (blocker A1 and the seven minors)

**A1 blocker — untranslated captions.** The five `code.token-caption` captions of the component
section and the type/border captions still rendered English words in German. Eight locale keys were
added in both files and wired with `data-i18n`; code, token names and units stay literal and the
sentence around them is German:

| Key | English | German |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components.captionBlock` | `--radius-lg · --card · grows in height` | `--radius-lg · --card · wächst in der Höhe` |
| `components.captionZone` | `--radius-lg · tone colour · dashed border` | `--radius-lg · Tonfarbe · gestrichelter Rahmen` |
| `components.captionConnection` | `edge · --tone-d · 1.5 px` | `Verbindung · --tone-d · 1.5 px` |
| `components.captionSidePanel` | `400 px · --header-height · serif title` | `400 px · --header-height · Titel in Serif` |
| `components.captionToolbar` | `48 px bar · 36 px buttons · 20 px icons` | `48-px-Leiste · 36-px-Knöpfe · 20-px-Symbole` |
| `type.captionLineHeight` | `--font-sans · --text-13 · line-height --line-height` | `… · Zeilenhöhe --line-height` |
| `type.captionTooltip` | `Tooltip · --text-12 · --weight-medium` | `Kurzhinweis · --text-12 · --weight-medium` |
| `space.captionOutlineWidth` | `--outline-width 2 px + offset` | `--outline-width 2 px + Versatz` |

The DOM coverage probe below now reports **0 mismatches and 0 uncovered English text/attributes** in
German: every `data-i18n*` hook equals the German value, every visible text node is either covered or
an identifier/token/unit value, and no `aria-label`/`alt`/`title`/`data-label` is left untranslated.

**Minor 1 — switch target size.** Each option is now a 32 × 32 px minimum target
(`min-inline-size`/`min-block-size: --click-target`) with 8 px horizontal padding (`--space-8`,
measured 33 × 32 px); the pill around both options is 70 × 34 px (32 px option plus the two 1 px
`--border` borders). README and this log carry the measured sizes, not the brief's 8 × 12 px padding
claim.

**Minor 2 — fallback/toggle consistency.** `preview.js` tracks the language that is really applied.
A failed locale load no longer touches the page: requesting `en.json` while German is active leaves
the page German on `DE`, requesting `de.json` while English is active leaves it English on `EN`. Only
on the first load, when nothing has been applied yet, the page settles once on the English markup
fallback (or on `locales/en.json` when it loads), so the switch never shows a language the page does
not display. No retry loop, no console error.

**Minor 3 — README.** Stale "English aria-label/alt" claims removed; the real fallback behaviour is
documented; the "hard reload may be needed for an already-cached `index.html`" wording was added to
the cache-bust section; `tokens.css` is versioned too (`tokens.css?v=P0-27`) and the icon SVGs are
explicitly documented as stable/unversioned; the last-change rule now says the line follows the
`P0-*` preview tasks (P0-19 … P0-27, P1-07) while the engine tasks `P4-*` run in parallel and do not
move it.

**Minor 4 — DE desktop screenshot.** The 1440 × 900 desktop captures are taken after scrolling the
page so the **whole demo surface** is visible (surface top 210, bottom 570 inside the 900 px
viewport); no card, photo or toolbar pixel is clipped. The layout itself is unchanged.

**Minor 5 — glossary.** German terms now follow `docs/i18n/glossary.md`: Zeitstrahl (not Zeitachse),
Seitenpanel (not Seitenleiste), Leinwand (not Canvas) — checked by script (`banned glossary terms in
de: []`).

## Port and server

Slot values (`.polier-slot`): `web=4200` for slot 2; the port is read from `.polier-slot`, never
hard-coded. Only this task's server and Chrome were started and both were stopped afterwards.

```sh
cd "/Users/rasulatashev/Desktop/KI Projekte/Project air-P0-27"
PORT=$(python3 -c "import json;print(json.load(open('.polier-slot'))['ports']['web'])")
python3 -m http.server "$PORT" --bind 127.0.0.1
```

Served the **repository root** so the relative token, icon, image and locale paths resolve. The
locales are fetched relative to the page, so the switch needs HTTP; from `file://` the page keeps the
English fallback (`<html lang="en">`).

