## Cache-busting check

```
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:4200/apps/web/preview/ | grep -nE '(tokens\.css|preview\.(css|js))\?v='
7:    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../../packages/ui-kit/tokens.css?v=P0-27" />
8:    <link rel="stylesheet" href="preview.css?v=P0-27" />
9:    <script src="preview.js?v=P0-27" defer></script>
```

- All three asset URLs (shared token stylesheet, preview stylesheet, preview script) carry
  `?v=P0-27` and return `200` with the current byte sizes; a browser that cached an older stylesheet
  requests a new URL and gets the current files.
- `preview.js` reads the `v` query of its own script URL and appends it to the locale requests
  (`locales/en.json?v=P0-27`, `locales/de.json?v=P0-27`, both `200`), so one bump covers the
  translations too.
- The icon SVGs keep stable, unversioned URLs (they only change with design-system tasks, which bump
  this version anyway).
- The README documents the bump rule and the one case the version query cannot fix: an already
  cached `index.html` (hard reload needed once).

